WEBVTT

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:03.020
The World Duel Carnival finally started!

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:10.320
Duelists from around the world have gathered in Heartland City
to battle and become the champion!

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:12.990
I’m gonna win it all!

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.990
Here I go! Kattobing!

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:18.990
Who are you?

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:22.960
This ball chose you.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:26.040
Let’s duel!

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.000
What’s with that ball?

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:31.150
It’s my friend.

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:37.470
I create my deck strategies
while juggling this ball tens of thousands of times.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.930
He put cards on his ball?

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:43.430
Wager your Heart Piece
and battle me!

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:48.780
Fine with me! I accept!

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:51.360
I’m Yuma Tsukumo! Who are you?

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:53.610
Kakeru Kunitachi!

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:55.330
Kakeru Kunitachi?

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:56.620
You know him?

00:00:57.230 --> 00:00:59.530
I heard that name before.

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:01.870
It’s starting?

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:06.330
It’s time for the kickoff!

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:10.280
All right! I’m kattobing!

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:12.960
Duel Disk set!

00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:22.470
D-Gazer set!

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:27.690
AR Vision Link complete.

00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:29.270
Duel!

00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:30.770
I’ll go first!

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:32.610
My turn! I draw!

00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:38.280
I set a monster in defense
position and end my turn!

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:41.490
You set Gogogo Golem.

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:47.960
I thought you would lose your cool and summon
a monster in attack position without thinking about the future.

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:50.500
You’ve matured a bit.

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:53.920
Be quiet! Stop talking and watch!

00:01:54.470 --> 00:02:01.860
I don’t know who you’re arguing with,
but you’ll be quiet after witnessing the power of my soccer deck.

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:02.600
Here I go!

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:04.600
My turn! I draw!

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:08.310
I activate the Field
Spell Stadium of Dreams!

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.910
What’s this?

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:35.570
What’s this?

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:39.350
What’s going on?

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:43.810
We’re suddenly
in a large soccer stadium!

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:48.310
To summarize, this is the Field
Spell Stadium of Dreams’s effect?

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:53.560
Wow!

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:54.960
That’s not all.

00:02:54.960 --> 00:03:00.410
Stadium of Dreams switches monsters
from face-down defense position to face-up defense position!

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:01.320
What?

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:09.210
Then I summon Wing
Captain from my hand!

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:17.440
1100 ATK?

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:20.380
Its attack won’t work
against Gogogo Golem!

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:23.850
I activate the spell
card Perfect Pass!

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:26.310
Receive it, Wing Captain!

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:34.740
If Wing Captain battles a monster
with higher DEF this turn, its ATK is doubled!

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:38.010
Go ahead and double
or triple its ATK!

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:43.030
Due to Gogogo Golem’s effect,
it can’t be destroyed in battle once per turn!

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:43.960
Not good enough.

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:47.700
Perfect Pass negates your
battling monster’s effects!

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:48.720
What?

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:53.170
Go, Wing Captain! Ultra Bullet Shot!

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:08.310
Why?

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:12.560
If you destroy my monster while it’s
in defense position, you can’t take away my LP!

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:19.230
If Wing Captain’s ATK are greater than your DEF,
its effect deals the difference as damage!

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:23.180
Damn! This guy is tough!

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:26.900
I reached my hand towards

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:30.080
The light that shines to tomorrow

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:37.040
I dreamed of the world
that spreads beneath my feet

00:04:40.930 --> 00:04:46.300
I don’t know where dreams
and hope are located

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:50.890
No matter how much I search,
I can’t find them

00:04:51.860 --> 00:04:56.930
Maybe it fell into
the space between truth and lies

00:04:57.560 --> 00:05:02.110
Our story hasn’t started yet

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:07.430
The road to tomorrow
seems like it will crumble

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:13.000
But let’s go
before we lose heart

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:16.070
As we come closer,
it moves further away

00:05:16.070 --> 00:05:18.840
In order to seize the truth

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:24.470
We’ll search for hope
in the unseen future

00:05:24.470 --> 00:05:27.170
Our hearts are stronger
than everyone else’s

00:05:27.170 --> 00:05:30.450
We’ll carry it
within us and go

00:05:30.450 --> 00:05:36.060
Fight weakness to have
the strength to win

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:38.020
In order to find it

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:41.480
Along with my irreplaceable friends

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:47.990
I saw tomorrow in the world
that spreads beneath my feet

00:05:57.500 --> 00:06:01.920
I set one card
and end my turn!

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:06.080
Do your best, Yuma!
The duel is only getting started!

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:07.310
Fight!

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:15.020
\hWDC Kickoff! The Flaming Striker, Kakeru Kunitachi\h

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:15.020
Number 27

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:09.410
The battle starts now!

00:06:09.410 --> 00:06:11.260
Yuma, cattabing!

00:06:12.610 --> 00:06:15.020
They’re right. Okay, here I go!

00:06:15.380 --> 00:06:17.990
My turn! I draw!

00:06:17.990 --> 00:06:21.230
I summon Gagaga Magician!

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:25.150
Go, Gagaga Magician!

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:27.280
Attack Wing Captain!

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:31.380
Good! Gagaga Magician has 1500 ATK!

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:34.740
Wing Captain’s ATK returned
to normal, so...

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:41.420
He did it!

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:42.380
Goal!

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:44.590
You did it, Yuma!

00:06:46.910 --> 00:06:48.630
The goal doesn’t count.

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:50.310
Doesn’t count?

00:06:50.310 --> 00:06:51.050
Why?

00:06:51.480 --> 00:06:52.780
It’s a trap card.

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:53.550
Trap?

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:58.310
Yes. I activated
the trap card Offside Trap.

00:06:58.310 --> 00:06:59.770
Offside?

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:08.190
When a monster on my field is destroyed, that monster’s
destruction and damage are negated, and the turn ends.

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:10.660
The turn ends?

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:12.410
No way!

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:17.910
Observation #15: Soccer is very deep.

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:21.080
This isn’t the time
to admire it!

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:24.290
It’s about time I get real.

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:27.280
My turn! I draw!

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:29.970
I summon Top Scorer!

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:37.250
He summoned a Level 5 monster
without tributing another monster?

00:07:37.250 --> 00:07:38.770
You’re not allowed to do that!

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:45.150
When the Field Spell Stadium of Dreams is active,
I can summon Top Scorer without tributing!

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:47.020
You’ve gotta be kidding!

00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:49.490
Go, Top Scorer!

00:07:49.870 --> 00:07:52.450
Attack Gagaga Magician!

00:07:57.420 --> 00:08:01.250
Your goal is empty!
Go, Wing Captain!

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:03.540
Attack him directly!

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:12.130
Yuma!

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:14.050
I can’t watch!

00:08:14.630 --> 00:08:15.850
I’m not done.

00:08:15.850 --> 00:08:19.310
I activate the spell
card Eye Contact!

00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:24.010
Its effect lets me return Offside Trap
from my graveyard to my hand!

00:08:24.010 --> 00:08:27.980
I set one card
and end my turn.

00:08:27.980 --> 00:08:29.410
What should I do?

00:08:29.410 --> 00:08:38.030
If he uses Offside Trap again,
he’ll negate my attack and end my turn!

00:08:38.490 --> 00:08:40.230
Why are you sleeping?

00:08:40.230 --> 00:08:42.440
I’m not sleeping.

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:46.250
I’m trying to remember
what soccer is.

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:51.710
I can’t count on you at all!
What should I do?

00:08:51.710 --> 00:08:53.700
Thinking is worthless.

00:08:53.700 --> 00:08:56.250
My soccer deck has no weaknesses.

00:08:56.250 --> 00:08:58.250
There’s no way you can win!

00:08:58.250 --> 00:08:59.650
Hey, look!

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:02.930
Is this real?
I’m a huge fan!

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:10.230
It’s Kaz and Hide, two brothers who start
and play the striker position for the soccer team!

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:12.320
Why are they here?

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:14.730
Now I know who he is!

00:09:14.730 --> 00:09:16.030
He’s Kakeru Kunitachi!

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:20.840
To summarize, he’s Kaz
and Hide’s younger brother!

00:09:22.900 --> 00:09:30.750
He’s the third son of Shigeru Kunitachi,
the famous world-class coach who executes perfect team play!

00:09:30.750 --> 00:09:34.470
Really? You’re the youngest member
of that famous soccer family?

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:39.180
So what? I have nothing to do
with my dad or my brothers!

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:41.110
Who cares about team play?

00:09:41.110 --> 00:09:44.140
I’ve had enough
of others holding me back!

00:09:44.140 --> 00:09:46.550
That’s why I chose dueling.

00:09:46.550 --> 00:09:48.650
Dueling is a one-on-one battle!

00:09:48.650 --> 00:09:52.110
When I’m standing on the field,
I can only trust myself!

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:53.280
Just watch!

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:57.060
I’ll use my own power
to become duel champion!

00:09:57.060 --> 00:09:59.660
You’re wrong, Kakeru!

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:01.620
Dueling is also team play!

00:10:02.030 --> 00:10:03.620
Team play?

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:05.750
You’re not alone right now.

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:07.980
You’re battling alongside your teammates!

00:10:07.980 --> 00:10:09.330
Teammates?

00:10:09.330 --> 00:10:12.670
Yeah. Wing Captain and Top Scorer.

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:15.340
Those monsters are your teammates!

00:10:16.510 --> 00:10:20.190
While I battle, I always
believe in my monsters.

00:10:20.190 --> 00:10:23.260
My monsters
and I form one team!

00:10:23.740 --> 00:10:26.480
Team?

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:29.380
Let’s go, Yuma. It’s our turn.

00:10:29.750 --> 00:10:32.480
So you now remember soccer?

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:36.720
Yes. And thanks to you,
I came up with a good idea.

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:37.940
Let’s win!

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:45.720
We can’t afford to lose.

00:10:45.720 --> 00:10:48.290
Of course! Here I go!

00:10:48.680 --> 00:10:51.410
My turn! I draw!

00:10:51.410 --> 00:10:52.330
I—

00:10:52.720 --> 00:10:54.500
I summon Zubaba Buster!

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:59.010
I’m going to summon it!

00:10:59.010 --> 00:11:01.970
I summon Zubaba Buster!

00:11:06.850 --> 00:11:12.150
Then I use the spell card Monster Reborn
to Special Summon Gogogo Golem!

00:11:13.060 --> 00:11:14.570
Gogogo Golem?

00:11:14.960 --> 00:11:17.570
It’s team play, Yuma. Trust me.

00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:19.680
Fine!

00:11:19.680 --> 00:11:22.990
I activate the spell
card Monster Reborn!

00:11:23.460 --> 00:11:26.990
I Special Summon Gogogo Golem
from my graveyard in defense position!

00:11:28.110 --> 00:11:32.830
No matter what monster you summon,
you can’t beat my Offside Trap!

00:11:33.620 --> 00:11:35.890
If he activates it again...

00:11:35.890 --> 00:11:37.780
Use Cross Attack, Yuma.

00:11:38.150 --> 00:11:41.940
Activate the spell card
Cross Attack from your hand.

00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:43.800
I see!

00:11:44.170 --> 00:11:47.310
I activate the spell
card Cross Attack!

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:55.750
When there are two monsters on the field with the same ATK, I can attack the opponent directly!

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:05.820
He scored a goal on me.

00:12:06.270 --> 00:12:09.830
He did it! It’s
his first goal!

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:11.460
He did it!

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:15.500
Team Yuma took LP away
from Kakeru!

00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:16.560
Damn!

00:12:16.560 --> 00:12:20.670
He found out that Offside Trap can’t
activate against direct attacks!

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:22.410
I’m not done.

00:12:22.410 --> 00:12:30.270
When Zubaba Buster deals you damage,
your monster with the lowest ATK is destroyed!

00:12:32.030 --> 00:12:39.980
Zubaba Buster loses 800 ATK when it uses this effect,
but destroying your monster is worth it.

00:12:40.570 --> 00:12:42.050
I can also use this!

00:12:42.050 --> 00:12:44.990
I activate the Quick-Play
Spell Extra Blast!

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:51.040
When an effect destroys your monster,
you take 500 points of damage!

00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:54.800
They’re tied!

00:12:54.800 --> 00:12:56.210
He caught up!

00:12:57.150 --> 00:12:59.210
You did it, Yuma!

00:12:59.210 --> 00:13:02.670
See that? That’s my team play!

00:13:02.670 --> 00:13:05.780
I set one card
and end my turn!

00:13:07.310 --> 00:13:10.180
Don’t get overconfident, Yuma Tsukumo!

00:13:10.180 --> 00:13:13.930
Wing Captain is a lame monster
with only 1100 ATK.

00:13:13.930 --> 00:13:16.400
I don’t care if that
useless card gets destroyed!

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:19.290
You’re still talking like that?

00:13:19.290 --> 00:13:22.610
You have to trust your monsters
because they’re your teammates!

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:25.610
The useless aren’t my teammates!

00:13:28.060 --> 00:13:29.120
Over here!

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:30.480
Pass it!

00:13:31.390 --> 00:13:34.200
What are you doing? You’re useless!

00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:36.770
Hurry up and
get me the ball!

00:13:36.770 --> 00:13:38.630
Sheesh...

00:13:40.140 --> 00:13:42.380
I’ll do it myself!

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:43.960
Over here!

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:48.640
Kakeru, pass it to me!

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:52.770
I don’t trust you!
I’ll do it by myself!

00:14:00.400 --> 00:14:02.660
That’s Kaz and Hide’s younger brother?

00:14:02.660 --> 00:14:04.860
He’s so much worse
than his brothers.

00:14:05.990 --> 00:14:10.780
I heard that he hurt his leg,
but maybe he has no talent.

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:13.700
Are you okay, Kakeru?

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:15.810
Be quiet!

00:14:15.810 --> 00:14:17.660
You couldn’t mark them!

00:14:17.660 --> 00:14:19.610
You’re useless!

00:14:19.610 --> 00:14:22.170
You’re the useless one, Kakeru!

00:14:22.170 --> 00:14:24.310
You can’t play soccer alone!

00:14:24.310 --> 00:14:27.130
If you can’t understand that,
leave the field!

00:14:29.110 --> 00:14:32.430
After that day,
I gave up on soccer.

00:14:32.800 --> 00:14:38.730
I vowed to triumph
over my brothers someday.

00:14:39.850 --> 00:14:43.070
And I’ll do that by dueling!

00:14:43.070 --> 00:14:45.860
Dueling allows me to become
a world champion by myself!

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:48.030
Be honest with yourself, Kakeru.

00:14:48.990 --> 00:14:51.470
I know you realize it too.

00:14:51.470 --> 00:14:55.490
If you didn’t, you couldn’t have built
that powerful soccer deck.

00:14:55.850 --> 00:14:58.710
That’s your all-star team.

00:14:58.710 --> 00:15:02.130
Kakeru, you love soccer!

00:15:02.980 --> 00:15:05.340
Be quiet! I don’t care
about soccer!

00:15:05.760 --> 00:15:08.310
It’s okay to love
what you love!

00:15:08.310 --> 00:15:09.920
I love dueling.

00:15:09.920 --> 00:15:13.050
That’s why I’ll battle
with my friends to the end!

00:15:14.360 --> 00:15:17.390
Friends... Team...

00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:20.760
I... You...

00:15:21.790 --> 00:15:23.340
I...

00:15:24.020 --> 00:15:27.230
My turn! I draw!

00:15:27.230 --> 00:15:29.950
I’ll trust them!

00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:33.700
I summon Defending
Sweeper from my hand!

00:15:35.510 --> 00:15:40.830
When Stadium of Dreams is on the field,
this monster gains 1 Level!

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:44.290
Then I activate
the spell card All For One!

00:15:44.290 --> 00:15:47.950
So you did have that card!

00:15:47.950 --> 00:15:49.750
This isn’t the time to celebrate.

00:15:49.750 --> 00:15:55.600
With that spell card, when he has two monsters on his field
with the same Type and Level...

00:15:55.600 --> 00:16:00.020
...he can Special Summon a monster
from his graveyard with the same Type.

00:16:00.020 --> 00:16:03.500
I bring back Wing Captain!

00:16:08.150 --> 00:16:12.880
The Special Summoned
monster gains 1 Level.

00:16:14.070 --> 00:16:17.410
He has three Level 5
monsters! That means...

00:16:17.850 --> 00:16:22.920
I overlay Level 5 Top Scorer,
Defending Sweeper and Wing Captain!

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:28.210
With these three monsters,
I build the Overlay Network!

00:16:28.210 --> 00:16:29.550
Xyz Summon!

00:16:29.970 --> 00:16:33.050
You’re up, Playmaker!

00:16:40.470 --> 00:16:42.580
2600 ATK?

00:16:42.580 --> 00:16:45.810
To summarize, Yuma is finished
if he takes the attack!

00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:48.320
Go! Attack Zubaba Buster!

00:16:48.320 --> 00:16:50.280
Yuma, use your trap card!

00:16:50.280 --> 00:16:55.740
I activate the trap card Half Unbreak
and target Zubaba Buster!

00:16:57.700 --> 00:17:01.660
Its effect prevents Zubaba Buster
from being destroyed!

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:04.160
Ole Ole Drive Shot!

00:17:09.640 --> 00:17:14.300
Due to Half Unbreak’s effect,
I only take half the damage!

00:17:14.300 --> 00:17:20.200
You were willing to lose LP
to protect your monster teammate.

00:17:20.200 --> 00:17:21.890
But it isn’t over yet!

00:17:22.340 --> 00:17:24.890
I activate Playmaker’s effect!

00:17:24.890 --> 00:17:31.480
By using one Overlay Unit,
it can attack your monster with the highest ATK again!

00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:38.540
Gogogo Golem can’t be destroyed
in battle once per turn!

00:17:45.810 --> 00:17:47.710
It can’t survive a second attack!

00:17:57.040 --> 00:18:01.970
I use the final Overlay Unit
to attack for a third time!

00:18:01.970 --> 00:18:04.740
Only Zubaba Buster is left!

00:18:04.740 --> 00:18:06.180
Go, Playmaker!

00:18:06.180 --> 00:18:08.600
Ole Ole Drive Shot!

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:12.770
Half Unbreak’s effect is still active!

00:18:18.310 --> 00:18:20.070
Yuma!

00:18:20.650 --> 00:18:24.200
You managed to survive,
but you only have 100 LP left.

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:26.490
I’ll finish you
on my next turn!

00:18:26.490 --> 00:18:28.010
I end my turn.

00:18:28.010 --> 00:18:30.830
Don’t worry, Kotori.

00:18:30.830 --> 00:18:35.980
The Duel Carnival is awesome
because I can battle powerful duelists like him!

00:18:35.980 --> 00:18:38.380
You think you’re going to win?

00:18:38.380 --> 00:18:41.470
I still have Offside Trap.

00:18:41.470 --> 00:18:45.430
I can win because
I believe in my teammates!

00:18:47.230 --> 00:18:48.190
Here I go!

00:18:48.190 --> 00:18:50.190
My turn! I draw!

00:18:50.620 --> 00:18:53.610
I summon Gagaga Girl!

00:19:02.120 --> 00:19:04.080
1000 ATK?

00:19:04.080 --> 00:19:06.180
It’s pointless to summon that monster—

00:19:06.830 --> 00:19:09.330
Actually, he now
has Level 3 monsters...

00:19:09.330 --> 00:19:11.090
Go, Yuma!

00:19:11.090 --> 00:19:13.420
Summon a new Xyz Monster!

00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:14.040
Yeah!

00:19:14.040 --> 00:19:19.080
I overlay Level 3 Zubaba Buster
and Gagaga Girl!

00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:23.490
With these two monsters,
I build the Overlay Network!

00:19:23.490 --> 00:19:25.310
Xyz Summon!

00:19:25.310 --> 00:19:28.280
Come, wandering guitarist!

00:19:29.810 --> 00:19:31.940
This is my new teammate!

00:19:32.550 --> 00:19:34.750
Muzurhythm!

00:19:40.740 --> 00:19:45.160
Then I activate
the Equip Spell Giant Hunter!

00:19:45.160 --> 00:19:47.910
I equip it on to Muzurhythm!

00:19:47.910 --> 00:19:55.630
Due to this card’s effect, the opponent can’t activate spell
or trap cards until the end of the Battle Phase!

00:19:56.380 --> 00:19:59.540
Oh no! I can’t
use Offside Trap!

00:19:59.540 --> 00:20:03.840
When the monster equipped
with Giant Hunter attacks...

00:20:03.840 --> 00:20:09.410
...if I have less LP than you,
your monster’s ATK is halved!

00:20:09.410 --> 00:20:11.270
Its ATK is halved?

00:20:11.270 --> 00:20:14.520
Then I activate Muzurhythm’s effect!

00:20:14.950 --> 00:20:22.370
By using one Overlay Unit, its ATK is doubled
when it battles your Xyz Monster!

00:20:22.370 --> 00:20:25.340
Finish ’em, Muzurhythm!

00:20:37.710 --> 00:20:39.210
Goal!

00:20:39.210 --> 00:20:42.230
Team Yuma manages a come-from-behind victory!

00:20:42.230 --> 00:20:43.720
He did it!

00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:47.180
Yuma won!

00:20:47.180 --> 00:20:49.010
Yuma, you won.

00:20:49.010 --> 00:20:52.650
With a little help from you.

00:21:03.530 --> 00:21:04.990
You...

00:21:04.990 --> 00:21:10.470
It’s been a long time since
I played soccer with such passion.

00:21:10.470 --> 00:21:12.950
Soccer really is fun!

00:21:12.950 --> 00:21:14.410
Soccer?

00:21:14.830 --> 00:21:16.140
Right?

00:21:16.140 --> 00:21:17.130
Yeah!

00:21:17.130 --> 00:21:20.220
I actually love soccer!

00:21:20.220 --> 00:21:22.580
Thanks to you,
I came to my senses.

00:21:23.640 --> 00:21:27.460
If that’s how you feel,
then come back, Kakeru.

00:21:27.460 --> 00:21:29.220
Back to our field.

00:21:29.220 --> 00:21:30.640
Brothers!

00:21:30.640 --> 00:21:35.980
You should now be able to
understand what we were talking about.

00:21:35.980 --> 00:21:38.160
What you said back then...

00:21:38.160 --> 00:21:41.090
That you don’t play soccer alone.

00:21:43.650 --> 00:21:45.480
It all worked out, Kakeru!

00:21:45.480 --> 00:21:46.320
Yeah!

00:21:46.320 --> 00:21:50.880
I’m going to practice hard at soccer so that
I can quickly catch up to my brothers!

00:21:50.880 --> 00:21:53.910
I’ll also work hard
to become duel champion!

00:21:54.300 --> 00:21:56.870
It’s yours.

00:21:59.400 --> 00:22:02.380
All right! I got one!

00:22:02.380 --> 00:22:04.410
And I’ll win my next match!

00:22:04.410 --> 00:22:06.510
No matter
who the opponent, bring it on!

00:22:07.060 --> 00:22:10.100
I’m kattobing!

00:22:20.200 --> 00:22:23.360
Someone gave me water

00:22:23.730 --> 00:22:29.570
It easily created a rainbow

00:22:30.400 --> 00:22:35.200
To be who I want to be

00:22:36.000 --> 00:22:38.230
Is difficult

00:22:39.080 --> 00:22:41.750
Without struggle

00:22:41.750 --> 00:22:45.900
I can’t win

00:22:46.800 --> 00:22:48.700
But I want to bloom

00:22:49.050 --> 00:22:52.550
I have a dream
that’s not cool

00:22:53.130 --> 00:22:56.200
In order to achieve it

00:22:56.660 --> 00:22:59.850
I don’t care
if you laugh at me

00:22:59.850 --> 00:23:06.800
I set my limits low

00:23:06.800 --> 00:23:09.910
So I’ll overcome it tomorrow

00:23:09.910 --> 00:23:14.240
Ah! Aiming for the blue skies

00:23:14.240 --> 00:23:15.600
In full bloom

00:23:15.600 --> 00:23:17.830
Yearning freesia

00:23:19.580 --> 00:23:23.370
Countless petals

00:23:23.370 --> 00:23:26.230
Were sacrificed

00:23:26.920 --> 00:23:30.180
I’m above them

00:23:30.180 --> 00:23:34.300
Ah! Lost my way again today

00:23:34.300 --> 00:23:36.040
I admire

00:23:36.040 --> 00:23:37.830
Yearning freesia

00:23:41.060 --> 00:23:48.900
My second opponent in the Duel Carnival may be physically small, but he uses heavy machinery monsters!

00:23:48.900 --> 00:23:52.740
This gigantic structure
is connected together by small pieces.

00:23:54.200 --> 00:23:56.330
What a humongous monster!

00:23:56.330 --> 00:23:57.080
Yuma, watch out!

00:23:57.680 --> 00:24:02.240
Shobe, I’ll show you
that dueling isn’t just about power!

00:24:02.250 --> 00:24:10.050
\h\hConstruction Site Duel! Defeat the Heavy Machinery Deck!!\h\h

00:24:02.250 --> 00:24:07.340
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZEXAL:
“Construction Site Duel! Defeat the Heavy Machinery Deck!!”

00:24:07.340 --> 00:24:10.050
I’m kattobing!

00:24:10.770 --> 00:24:15.010
I almost made
a three-pointer in today’s duel!

00:24:15.010 --> 00:24:18.140
That’s basketball.
It’s called a “smash” in soccer.

00:24:18.140 --> 00:24:19.680
That’s tennis.

00:24:20.160 --> 00:24:21.270
Then I should call it
an “attack?”

00:24:21.270 --> 00:24:23.430
I don’t care anymore.
